      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] This test suite setup is fantastic! I see you added comprehensive coverage for the main success and error paths. \n\nHowever, it looks like a test for the uninitialized state (calling `enroll_step` without calling `enroll_start`) was missed. Since that was the original bug that motivated adding this test harness, it would be great to include it to prevent future regressions.\n\nYou could add something like this:\n```c\nZTEST_F(ft98xx_bio_alg, test_enroll_step_without_start)\n{\n\tint completion \u003d -1;\n\n\tzassert_ok(fingerprint_algorithm_init(fixture-\u003ealg));\n\n\t/* Do not call fingerprint_enroll_start to simulate the bypass */\n\tint res \u003d fingerprint_enroll_step(fixture-\u003ealg, fixture-\u003efake_image,\n\t\t\t\t\t  \u0026completion);\n\n\tzassert_equal(res, FP_ENROLLMENT_RESULT_INTERNAL_ERROR,\n\t\t      \"enroll_step should fail if enroll_start wasn\u0027t called\");\n\tzassert_equal(completion, 0,\n\t\t      \"completion should be safely set to 0\");\n}\n```",
